{
 "_about": "v63: the general-part concepts a «cenni» subject may name, each with the articles that regulate it (src/rag/cenni.py). A subject matching a concept's pattern (lower case, any position) is a general concept: its cenni rest on these articles, never on a special-part article (c.p. Libro II/III) unless that article's rubrica names the subject itself («omicidio preterintenzionale» -> 43 and 584 c.p.). A concept is consulted only when its code is among the case's codes. Patterns are Python regular expressions. v64: elements, the patterns of a charged article's element that is of the concept's kind (nesso causale: «cagiona»; elemento soggettivo: «con atti diretti a», «per colpa») -- the concept's articles then get an «applicazione» paragraph for the defence (src/rag/cenni.element_refs). The mapping is Code's draft of doctrine, listed in docs/copy_review.md for the PO and the lawyer. v75: the procedural concepts («procedural»: true -- querela, sequestro, restituzione, parte civile): a procedural ask the first read or a cenni names resolves through this table (interactive_flow.first_read_search), never through a single-word rubrica hit («Confisca», «Querela»). v76: the protection asks -- divieto di avvicinamento (282-ter c.p.p.), allontanamento d'urgenza (384-bis c.p.p.), misure cautelari (272-275 c.p.p.), ammonimento del questore (art. 8 d.l. 11/2009; on the ingestion list until the corpus holds it).",
